+    /* BoxedVN: the terminal threshold, lowered from 2000.
+     *
+     * 2000 was chosen against storms that burned CPU and log space -- 65k,
+     * 70k, 326,500 redeliveries -- where the cost of waiting was time. It is
+     * the wrong shape for a storm that burns the GUEST STACK, because every
+     * redelivery pushes an exception frame onto it and the stack runs out
+     * first. Two device runs, with different root causes and different stack
+     * sizes, ended identically: the "256 identical redeliveries ... storm
+     * forming" line appears, the terminal line never does, and the run dies
+     * of STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW naming a guard page instead of the fault that
+     * caused it. One had a 1 MiB stack, the other 8 MiB; neither reached
+     * 2000. A threshold the stack cannot survive is not a guard.
+     *
+     * 512 is above anything legitimate and below anything fatal. The code
+     * already treats 256 as abnormal enough to warn about, and handled
+     * retries -- redirects, USD, unaligned -- never reach this point at all,
+     * so there is no pattern between 512 and 2000 that this now cuts short.
+     * What it buys is the forensic dump below running while there is still
+     * stack to run it on, which is the difference between a log that names
+     * the faulting pc and one that does not. */
+#define IOS_REDELIV_TERMINAL 512
+
